  "id": "bashkir_kubair_epic",
  "name": "Kubair (Bashkir sesen epic recitation)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Epic tradition of the Bashkirs of the southern Urals, in which sesen, improvising poet-singers, recited kubair, the Bashkir epic verse form, to tell epics such as Ural-batyr, the tale of a hero who defeats the divs and pours out the water of eternal life over the land instead of drinking it. Sesen delivered the verse in a chanted recitative and could accompany themselves on the dumbyra, a long-necked plucked lute represented here by the dombyra card; Ural-batyr was written down from sesen performance in the early twentieth century.",
  "recipe": "classic modern kubair, ballad Poetry. long necked teardrop bodied dombyra. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
